PART A - CORE COMPONENTS (APACHE-2.0)

A.1 Grant. Each Core Component is licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0, the full text of which is in the file LICENSE-APACHE-2.0 and at
https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0. Under that license you may use,
reproduce, modify, distribute, and sublicense Core Components for any
purpose, including commercial and production use, subject to its conditions
(including retaining notices and marking changes). You also receive the
patent license in its Section 3.

A.2 Contributions to Core. Unless you explicitly state otherwise, any
contribution you intentionally submit for inclusion in a Core Component is
licensed under Apache-2.0 as provided in Section 5 of that license.

A.3 Mixed files. Some Core files register, list, or integrate with
Simulation Components (for example, a module list that imports a Simulation
module, a privilege allowlist that names Simulation functions, or a test that
exercises both). Such a file is a Core Component in its entirety and is
licensed under Part A. Licensing that file does not license the Simulation
Component it refers to, and a reference to a Simulation Component is not a
copy of it.

A.4 Third-party material. Third-party dependencies are not part of this
repository's licensed work and remain under their own licenses.


